ARCHIPEPSI - DIAGNOSTIC CAMPAIGN, PRIVATE BUILD   (revision @REVISION@)

A private diagnostic build of the existing prototype-scale campaign, for hands-on review. It is not a release and not a release candidate. It starts the game and its bundled bridge together, so neither Godot nor Python needs installing.

HOW TO PLAY

  Double-click "START HERE - Mock Campaign (Windows).bat", or install the
  zip in the Archipepsi Launcher and press Play.

  On the title screen choose MOCK CAMPAIGN. That is the deterministic
  offline campaign: thirty Checks over about ten Zones, the fallback
  Epsilon, no server, no network, no API key.

  Closing the game also stops the bridge.

  "With log window - Mock Campaign (Windows).bat" is the same build with
  the bridge and the game printing into one window, for when something
  goes wrong and you want to watch it happen. (The launcher's own "log
  window" option starts the same thing.)

WHERE YOUR SAVE IS

  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Archipepsi\Diagnostic Campaign\saves   the campaign
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Archipepsi\Diagnostic Campaign\logs    bridge and starter logs
  %APPDATA%\Godot\app_userdata\Archipepsi               game settings and
                                                        loadout (Godot's own
                                                        folder, shared with a
                                                        checkout's Godot runs)

  Nothing is written into this build's folder, so deleting or replacing
  the build keeps your campaign. To start over, delete the "saves" folder
  above (paste the path into Explorer's address bar).

  This campaign is separate from a checkout's bridge\saves and from the
  checkout's diagnostic slots. It is the ordinary prototype-scale MOCK
  CAMPAIGN, without the --candidate profile and without any review room.

WHAT IS AND IS NOT IN THIS BUILD

  Included and tested:  the game (Godot 4.5.1 export), the bridge, a
                        private copy of Python 3.12 with the bridge's two
                        libraries, the offline MOCK CAMPAIGN.

  NOT included:         the real Archipelago connection. The bridge here
                        runs in mock mode only, exactly as the checkout's
                        "Start Archipepsi" does, so a server address typed
                        into the game connects to the offline mock
                        campaign, not to a server. Real Archipelago play
                        still needs the developer setup (an Archipelago
                        source checkout); it is untested in this form.

  Not included either:  the candidate generation profile (minors, carry,
                        lever routes, Bomb Bags), the review rooms
                        (Crossing D, Impact Lab, Impact Relay, the
                        Railway, 3A/3B), music, and any change to how the
                        campaign plays.

KNOWN LIMITATIONS

  - Built and tested on Linux, and run under Wine. Nobody has run it on
    native Windows yet; your hands-on review is that first run.
  - The executables are not code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen may say
    it "protected your PC". "More info" then "Run anyway" starts it.
  - If another Archipepsi bridge is already running (a checkout's "Start
    Archipepsi" window, say), this build refuses to start rather than
    play against that bridge's saves. Close the other one first.
  - The bridge banner reports its commit as "unknown": a packaged bridge
    has no git. This file's revision line and BUILD-INFO.txt say which
    commit it is.

WHAT IS IN THIS FOLDER

  Archipepsi-Diagnostic.exe          starts the bridge, then the game
  Archipepsi-Diagnostic.console.exe  the same, with a log window
  game\                              the Godot export (Archipepsi.exe)
  runtime\python\                    Python 3.12.10 (embeddable) + libraries
  runtime\bridge\                    the bridge, as committed at @REVISION@
  runtime\godot\content\registry\    room shells the bridge reads
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt            Godot, Python, library and runtime notices
  BUILD-INFO.txt                     source commit, toolchain, build command
  SHA256SUMS.txt                     a checksum for every file here
  archipepsi-build.json              the launcher's build description
